Origin: EmberBSD, AI-assisted.
pkgsrc/versions.mk keeps Rails 8.1 only; the EmberBSD recipes add the
Rails 8.1.4 packages and www/ruby-action_text-trix. rails.mk offers,
accepts and defaults to 81, and a package that accepts only an older
Rails gets a fail reason instead of a parse error. Move the packages that
accepted 7.2 or 8.0 onto 8.1: metasploit-model 5.0.6 and
metasploit-concern 5.0.7 allow Rails < 9; repofetch 0.5.2 and xdr 3.0.3,
the last releases, have their Rails upper bounds relaxed with
OVERRIDE_GEMSPEC. Bump PKGREVISION where the Rails dependency changes and
the package name does not.
Not submitted upstream.

